---
module: resource_loading
func_id: reject-prohibited-characters
---

***conformance tests***

# clean-value-passes
With `t.plain` holding `{% raw %}{{ v | prohibited_chars: '#' }}{% endraw %}`, rendering `{% raw %}{% include 't.plain', v: 5 %}{% endraw %}` gives `5`.

***acceptance tests***

# prohibited-character
With the same `t.plain`, rendering `{% raw %}{% include 't.plain', v: 'a#b' %}{% endraw %}` raises `InvalidLiquidVariableName` with `'#' is not a valid character for variable 'v' (value: 'a#b').`.
